    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">In the 1930s, Foshan thrives as the hub of Chinese kung fu, with various sects actively recruiting disciples. Though Ip Man (Donnie Yen) is an accomplished martial arts master, he keeps a low profile and only quietly sparring with his compatriots in friendly competitions at his home. But after an acknowledged victory to Jin Shan Zhao&apos;s (Fan Siu Wong) challenge, Ip Man becomes an instant hero and then develops a craze for Wing Chun in Foshan. Following the Japanese invasion, Ip Man&apos;s property is confiscated and his family is forced to live in a decrepit house. One day, General Miura (Hiroyuki Ikeuchi), a fanatical practitioner in martial arts, demands Ip Man to teach the Japanese Army Wing Chun, but Ip Man refuses it to his face and takes up Miura&apos;s challenge. He has to protect Chinese dignity by winning with Wing Chun.</marc:subfield>
    </marc:datafield>
